WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.756
Christians believe the Bible tells us true things about the world God made.

2
00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:15.054
We can also study that world for ourselves — telescopes, rocks and fossils, living things, the rules by which nature normally works.

3
00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:20.368
So we have God's Word, and we have God's world.

4
00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:23.024
They come from the same God.

5
00:00:23.024 --> 00:00:26.567
The question is how to understand them together.

6
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:35.779
Most scientists today say the universe is about thirteen point eight billion years old, and Earth about four and a half billion.

7
00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:41.719
The Bible seems to give us a much shorter story of creation and early history.

8
00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:45.283
Many Christians wonder what to do with that difference.

9
00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:48.847
Do we change the way we read the Bible?

10
00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:51.223
Do we reject what scientists see?

11
00:00:51.223 --> 00:00:53.995
Maybe those aren't our only choices.

12
00:00:53.995 --> 00:00:56.767
There's another question worth asking first.

13
00:00:57.267 --> 00:01:03.343
The Bible says God made the first man, Adam, as a grown man.

14
00:01:03.343 --> 00:01:06.614
Adam did not begin as a baby.

15
00:01:06.614 --> 00:01:13.625
Imagine a doctor meeting Adam the next day, with no idea God just made him.

16
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:19.234
The doctor examines his bones, teeth, muscles, organs — everything says grown man.

17
00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:21.571
That's a good observation.

18
00:01:21.571 --> 00:01:28.581
But if the doctor concludes this man spent years growing up, that would be wrong.

19
00:01:28.581 --> 00:01:30.918
Adam's body was mature.

20
00:01:30.918 --> 00:01:34.190
The years of growth had never happened.

21
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.929
What the doctor saw that day was real.

22
00:01:37.929 --> 00:01:40.733
The past he expected was not.

23
00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:47.528
The Gospel of John tells us Jesus turned water into wine at a wedding.

24
00:01:47.528 --> 00:01:54.272
Normally wine has a history — grapes grow, ripen, get picked and crushed, the juice ferments.

25
00:01:54.272 --> 00:01:58.318
That didn't happen to the wine Jesus made.

26
00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.116
It was real wine.

27
00:02:00.116 --> 00:02:04.612
Someone studying it could have measured what it was like.

28
00:02:04.612 --> 00:02:11.806
But those features didn't come from the normal history of growing grapes and making wine.

29
00:02:11.806 --> 00:02:14.503
Again — what was there was real.

30
00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:18.100
The usual history behind it had not happened.

31
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.207
Imagine starting a large video game.

32
00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:26.856
The computer builds a world by following rules — mountains, forests, rivers, caves, valleys.

33
00:02:26.856 --> 00:02:30.332
You enter one second after the world appears.

34
00:02:30.332 --> 00:02:34.243
There's a river flowing through a deep valley.

35
00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:38.153
Now imagine you're a scientist inside the game.

36
00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:52.492
You study the river, learn how fast water wears away rock, measure the valley, and work backward — you calculate the river would need ten thousand years of game time to carve that valley.

37
00:02:52.492 --> 00:02:54.665
Your math could be right.

38
00:02:54.665 --> 00:03:01.617
But there's one question it can't answer: did the river actually carve the valley?

39
00:03:01.617 --> 00:03:02.921
Maybe it did.

40
00:03:02.921 --> 00:03:09.004
Or maybe the computer made the river and valley together when the game began.

41
00:03:09.004 --> 00:03:12.046
The valley could be one second old.

42
00:03:12.046 --> 00:03:17.260
Working backward can tell us how long something would take to form.

43
00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:22.039
It cannot always tell us whether it actually formed that way.

44
00:03:22.039 --> 00:03:25.081
That doesn't prove Earth is young.

45
00:03:25.081 --> 00:03:32.033
It does mean a calculated age and an actual history aren't automatically the same thing.

46
00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:36.779
After the game world begins, things start happening inside it.

47
00:03:36.779 --> 00:03:42.724
Rivers keep cutting into their banks, trees grow, storms come, rocks fall, volcanoes erupt.

48
00:03:42.724 --> 00:03:46.120
Those become part of the game's history.

49
00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:58.434
So if you enter much later, you have a problem: some things were there when the game began, other things happened afterward — how can you tell which is which?

50
00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:03.953
You can't simply assume everything you see was there from the start.

51
00:04:03.953 --> 00:04:09.473
You also can't assume everything was made by the processes happening now.

52
00:04:09.473 --> 00:04:11.172
You have to investigate.

53
00:04:11.172 --> 00:04:16.267
We think the same question is worth asking about the real world.

54
00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:21.510
Every story about the universe has to start with something.

55
00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:31.946
The usual scientific story begins with a universe that already has matter, energy, and dependable rules, then a very long history follows.

56
00:04:31.946 --> 00:04:37.164
Genesis begins differently — God creates a world already ready to work.

57
00:04:37.164 --> 00:04:37.638
Light.

58
00:04:37.638 --> 00:04:39.062
Land and water.

59
00:04:39.062 --> 00:04:41.908
Plants and animals that can reproduce.

60
00:04:41.908 --> 00:04:45.703
The sun, moon, and stars doing their work.

61
00:04:45.703 --> 00:04:48.549
Human beings beginning as living people.

62
00:04:48.549 --> 00:04:53.292
The two stories may not begin at the same place.

63
00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:57.562
That could explain part of the disagreement about time.

64
00:04:57.562 --> 00:05:07.523
If God made a world already ready to work, working backward may go too far — it may pass the real beginning.

65
00:05:07.523 --> 00:05:18.433
Again, Adam gives us the simple picture: a doctor working backward from his adult body would describe years of growth that never happened.

66
00:05:18.933 --> 00:05:23.576
This doesn't mean everything we see was made at the beginning.

67
00:05:23.576 --> 00:05:31.699
After God created the world, real things happened — people lived, animals reproduced, rivers flowed, rock wore away, mud and sand moved.

68
00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:40.984
The Bible also tells us about Noah — his family and the animals with him were saved through a great Flood that covered the earth.

69
00:05:40.984 --> 00:05:48.334
If the Flood happened on the scale the Bible describes, it would have changed the ground in major ways.

70
00:05:48.334 --> 00:06:01.100
That gives us two questions worth investigating: what did the Flood do to the earth, and how can we tell the difference between what was there from the beginning and what happened later?

71
00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:05.154
Scientists have many ways of studying the past.

72
00:06:05.154 --> 00:06:16.703
One important method looks at atoms in rocks — some kinds slowly change into other kinds, and scientists measure how much has changed to calculate an age.

73
00:06:16.703 --> 00:06:18.480
The changes are real.

74
00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.256
The measurements are real.

75
00:06:20.256 --> 00:06:22.477
The calculation can be correct.

76
00:06:22.477 --> 00:06:28.252
But the same basic question remains: what was there when the rock began?

77
00:06:28.252 --> 00:06:34.471
If we know the starting point, working backward can tell us a great deal.

78
00:06:34.471 --> 00:06:42.466
If we assume the wrong starting point, the calculation may describe a history that didn't actually happen.

79
00:06:42.466 --> 00:06:49.573
That doesn't make scientific dating worthless — it tells us exactly what we need to investigate.

80
00:06:49.573 --> 00:06:52.239
What do we know from measurement?

81
00:06:52.239 --> 00:06:55.348
What are we assuming about the beginning?

82
00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:56.680
What happened afterward?

83
00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.567
And does the calculated history match the history that really happened?

84
00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:06.290
We don't claim to have solved every problem.

85
00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:12.860
There are hard questions about rocks, fossils, dating, heat, living things, and the stars.

86
00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:20.838
Some of our ideas may turn out to be wrong — if they do, we should say so.

87
00:07:20.838 --> 00:07:26.939
We shouldn't reject a real observation because it's difficult for us.

88
00:07:26.939 --> 00:07:34.917
We should also be careful not to confuse an explanation of an observation with the observation itself.

89
00:07:34.917 --> 00:07:37.263
The Bible is our authority.

90
00:07:37.263 --> 00:07:40.079
Our explanations of nature can improve.

91
00:07:40.079 --> 00:07:43.833
That's why this is an ongoing project.

92
00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:46.563
The basic idea is simple.

93
00:07:46.563 --> 00:07:48.347
God made the world.

94
00:07:48.347 --> 00:07:51.023
God also gave us His Word.

95
00:07:51.023 --> 00:07:58.159
The Bible tells us things about the beginning that no human being was there to watch.

96
00:07:58.159 --> 00:08:03.956
The world around us gives us things we can observe and measure today.

97
00:08:03.956 --> 00:08:06.632
We want to understand both together.

98
00:08:06.632 --> 00:08:15.998
That brings us to two questions: how much was already there when God made the world, and what happened after that?

99
00:08:15.998 --> 00:08:19.566
Those questions are the doorway into this project.

100
00:08:19.566 --> 00:08:23.133
We invite you to explore them with us.

101
00:08:23.633 --> 00:08:29.733
For deeper dives into exploring God's Word and God's World, visit odd Christian dot com.
